---
# The Purser interjects in every module of the prologue, at a different
# pressure. Component (dsl §13) because the beat is the same beat: a
# ship-voice line, over the announcement channel, reading the crew's draw
# against the shed schedule. The body is presentational — content lines and a
# param-scoped `<match on="@pressure">` (dsl 0.4.0 §6.2), which is the only
# logic block a component body admits.
component: purserInterject
params:
  pressure: string
# The component's own vocabulary import (dsl 0.9.0). It makes a STANDALONE
# `lute check` of this file resolve `emotion=`; through `::use` the IMPORTING
# document's vocabulary applies and this line is discarded at parse (0.9.0 §5,
# the known vocabulary-scope limitation), so BOTH sides must declare it.
uses: ../vocabulary.schema.yaml
---

## Interjection
<match on="@pressure">
<when is="rising">
@purser{code="0020" emotion="level" os}: Draw exceeds projection. The schedule advances.
</when>
<otherwise>
@purser{code="0010" emotion="level" os}: Allocation is nominal.
</otherwise>
</match>
